flowchart TD
  classDef works fill:#1d2029,stroke:#555b68,color:#eceef1;
  classDef friction fill:#262a34,stroke:#eceef1,stroke-width:2px,color:#eceef1;
  classDef broken fill:#1d2029,stroke:#d77757,stroke-width:2px,color:#d77757;
  classDef byhand fill:#1d2029,stroke:#eceef1,stroke-width:1px,stroke-dasharray:4 3,color:#eceef1;
  S1["1. The item shows the panda and the weekly<br/>percentage; semibold when over pace.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S2["2. Weekly: bar with the notch at the elapsed<br/>share, the reset and countdown, the status and<br/>projection, the allowance. Coral past the notch<br/>only when over pace.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S3["3. 5h window, the same five lines, for plans that<br/>have it.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S4["4. Open sessions by name (set with -n or /rename),<br/>by folder when unnamed, each with its model,<br/>its 24 cell context bar and '405.6k of 1M 41%';<br/>the figure's tooltip breaks over two lines<br/>inside the panel.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S5["5. Tokens by model, project or session with the<br/>price chip and the subagent share; click the<br/>switch or press m, p, s.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S6["6. Week over week: up to four rows, the current<br/>week 'so far', a hit week marked with the time<br/>it hit.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S7["7. With several sessions open the weekly figure<br/>holds still: the highest figure at the latest<br/>reset, across every session file.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S8["8. Esc closes, Tab and Shift Tab switch tabs,<br/>Command Q quits.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S9["9. The header says where the figures come from:<br/>'Live from Claude Code', 'As of 22:02, last<br/>Claude Code session', or 'Waiting for a Claude<br/>Code session'.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S10["10. After midnight the token rows stay: the first<br/>pass of a new day sums every record, not only<br/>new ones.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S11["11. On a short or scaled screen the panel stops 60<br/>points short of the screen's visible height and<br/>scrolls with an overlay scroller and no rubber<br/>band, from the top on every open and tab click;<br/>the keyboard focus scrolls into view, and a<br/>tooltip with no room above opens below its<br/>line.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S1 --> S2
  S2 --> S3
  S3 --> S4
  S4 --> S5
  S5 --> S6
  S6 --> S7
  S7 --> S8
  S8 --> S9
  S9 --> S10
  S10 --> S11
